codex
That context experiment does not heat because every `ValSeq`, including `intVals(IS)`, is already classified as a result. I’m reverting to the previously machine-checked two constructor-exposure rules. In the audit I’ll classify them explicitly as the operational definition of a new proof-input representation—not as a shortcut over a supplied iterator case—and keep their domain limited to the two exhaustive `IntSeq` constructors.
