codex
The independent audit is complete: the only execution-skipping rule is the loop summary, and its match domain is identical to a separately compiled bridge-free theorem, including arbitrary continuation and framed cells. The input representation unfolds one constructor and then hands control back to the supplied iterator; its two cases are exhaustive and separately checked. Gates A, B, and C therefore pass, so I’m writing `PROOF.md` with the `VALIDATED` headline.
